** Session 1: Two Altars and a Shop **


   I was pretty fresh off of playing "Ellora", an elven ranger, which
had gotten very far in the game. Once having acquired the spell of
Identify and Magic Mapping, the game had really opened up. I had
discovered many things with her, and felt quite confident that a
Wizard character would be able to progress just as far, and probably -
due to my new knowledge - I'd have an easier time with one.

   However, going from an extremely powerful character, to a beginning
one, is (was) quite a shock. <bewiderment> Elryk was slow, had very
few hit points, was easy to get hit, hardly an aresnal to speak of,
and consequently, very limited options when faced with opponents -
compared to my other character.

   Without a wonder whistle, or a leash, having a pet requires a
steady stream of patience. It took me a little while to get used to
this again. It had been nearly a year (in real time) since I've had to
do this.

   Exploration was slow. Grid bugs and jackals were to be feared.
These usually came in groups of three or four. Misericorde, proved to
be an invaluable asset. She was extremely fast, compared to my
character. Getting in several attacks for every round where I had a
chance to do something, or anything. Only times that were tense, was
when she was eating and there were still other monsters to dispatch.
Once; I had the wand of sleep at the ready. But she (luckily) came
through the round just before I was going to zap it.

   In the third room explored, I found one of them gray stones. I
patiently waited for Misericorde to dance over it several times before
picking it up. A necessary precaution. As; I just started this game,
and only have one scroll of Remove Curse.

   Nothing else of interest was found on the first level, but in the
room with the upstairs, on the second level, we discovered a studded
leather armor on the floor. Misericorde walked over it two times. I'm
now confident it isn't cursed...

AC:6 T:380

   Oh. That makes me feel much better!

   There was an altar to Ptah (lawful) on this level. It really did
not bother me that it didn't belong to Anhur. I now quite enjoy
desecrating the altars of other Gods, and increasing the strength of
my own God. <evil grin> I was getting hungry though, so needed to
press on in search of food. I'd be back here later on to put things
right (or wrong, depending on your point of view)...

   The third level down yielded a shop; Gaziantep's used armor
dealership.

   I piled all the goods in one spot so as to be able to copy down all
the information easier...

