T:868

   The hiking boots quickly filled me with hope that they might be
boots of speed, but Misericorde refused to step on them or pick them
up. Oh well, I'll be back here in the future when I'll be able to have
a better chance at trying to figure out what they are. I'm still not
finding enough food to hold me for long, and must press on. I think
that crude chain mail going for 168 zorkmids is magical. Too bad it
would hamper my spell casting ability. And besides, although I haven't
identified it as such yet - it's made by disgusting orcs.

   Found an altar to Thoth (neutral) while looking for food. I'll
desecrate this one too, but first I need some sustenance - quite
badly...

T:1003

   Okay, found a food ration and gobbled it down. Now looking for a
sacrificial corpse...

T:1182

   Damn. I can't find any. Where is a stupid orc when you need one,
eh?

   I'll be getting hungry again. I come to the conclusion that this,
for now, is just wasting my time.

   Oh well. I've done okay so far. Survived for over a thousand turns,
discovered two altars and a shop, and have explored the first three
levels.

   Another accomplishment was: That by this time, I had re-acquired
(or remembered) the "sense" (or "feel") of moving about with an
unleashed pet. I don't know how else to describe it. Nor can I give
you a specific method on how to do so. It's just something that one
develops after a while.

   I stop and save the game. Next session; I'll press on deeper with
the exploration of the Mazes of Menace.

   I'm sure that some of you won't find this session entertaining but,
to me, I felt quite satisfied with what I had accomplished.

